## Michael's Memo: When Speed and the Right Structure Both Matter

This month's client success story has many of the elements we see regularly in business funding requests.

Deadlines are tight. Construction timelines don't pause. Expected liquidity events don't always line up cleanly with real-world cash needs. In those moments, speed matters, but structure matters just as much.

This month's deal is a great example of how a proactive advisor, paired with the right capital source, can protect a company's long-term vision while solving a very short-term problem.

Let's keep serving well, together.

Here to serve,

Michael Kodinsky, Founder & CEO

## Deal Highlight: Mission-Critical Tier IV Data Center, Funded in Under Two Weeks

A seasoned data center developer with more than 20 years of experience building mission-critical infrastructure was nearing completion of a flagship Tier IV data center at its new headquarters campus in Central Florida. In the final phase, the team accelerated key workstreams to protect commissioning timelines and Tier IV performance standards, which introduced incremental costs tied to expedited execution.

Rather than slow progress or add long-term leverage at a critical moment, the company sought $1.5MM in short-term capital as a proactive bridge ahead of an anticipated liquidity event.

In under two weeks, Serve Funding structured and closed a flexible bridge facility built around the sponsor's capital plan: immediate liquidity for final-stage execution, a clean bridge to the upcoming equity injection, and a performance-based interest-forgiveness mechanism tied to early payoff that materially reduces total cost of capital once the liquidity event closes.

The full story is in the case study: [Subordinated Bridge for Data Center Operator](/blog/data-center-bridge-capital-case-study).

{% callout type="tip" title="The takeaway" %}
For experienced operators executing critical infrastructure projects, the right capital structure doesn't just solve a short-term need. It protects timelines, reputation, and long-term value.
{% /callout %}

## More Than Money: Core Value of the Month, Thankfulness

At Serve Funding, thankfulness is more than good manners. It's a posture of the heart. It shapes how we show up, how we build relationships, and how we serve.

We are genuinely grateful for the trust placed in us by the business owners we work with, by the advisors who introduce us, and by the lenders in our network who help us deliver timely, creative capital. That gratitude keeps us grounded and reminds us that every deal is more than a transaction. It represents a business, a vision, and people working hard to build something meaningful.

Thankfulness also strengthens the way we work. It helps us lead with humility, communicate with sincerity, and remain mindful that every introduction and every client conversation is a privilege. In a business built on relationships, gratitude keeps the human side of funding front and center.

This month, we want to sincerely thank you for your trust and for the opportunity to serve alongside you. We never take that lightly.
